WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.500
Every lead now has one owner,
with the reason on record.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.833
Now that owner writes. Outreach
drafts from your proof and your voice,

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:10.200
and sends only through guarded lanes.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.933
Nothing leaves without
a second pair of eyes.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.833
In this clip you'll build a draft,
read the gates, and approve a send.

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:21.767
One rule runs through all of it.
A send is an external effect,

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:25.967
so it is always a proposal that
a different human approves.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.033
Mia's team can write one good email.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:31.967
The hard part is every email
after that, each one true,

00:00:31.967 --> 00:00:37.033
each in the brand voice, and none to
someone who unsubscribed last week.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.267
First, a draft is grounded, not guessed.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:43.000
Outreach reads your brand voice, the
proof library for claims you can back,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.467
and customer phrases a person approved.
Personalization has three tiers.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:50.367
A one to one draft uses research,
proof and what has worked.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.233
A one to few draft uses a segment angle.

00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:55.100
One to many is a template
with no model call.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:59.900
The claims gate checks every factual
claim against active proof, twice:

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.567
when the send is proposed,
and again when it's sent.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:06.067
A claim with no proof, or
expired proof, blocks the send.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:10.400
In the console: Approvals, open an
approval, and read the Claims panel.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:13.267
Second, lanes. A lane is
where sending happens.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:16.300
It sets the channel, the
sending domain, a daily cap,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.767
and a touch window so nobody
is contacted twice in a row.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:23.867
Bounce and complaint thresholds
pause it. No active lane, no send.

00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:27.400
In the console: Engines, Outreach,
lanes and guardrail usage.

00:01:27.433 --> 00:01:31.400
More gates run when a send is proposed
and again when it's sent: Dry Mode,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.700
the engine's own mode, brand safety,
suppression, consent, reply stop,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.300
quiet hours and guardrail
caps. Then the net new rule.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.700
The first message to someone never
contacted always needs a human,

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.300
however much else is automated.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.867
If a send is held, ask your
agent: "Why was this send held? "

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.233
Here's a send end to end. Ask your agent:

00:01:49.233 --> 00:01:53.300
"Draft a one to one first touch to
Priya Nair at Northwind and propose it".

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.267
It drafts, grounds it,
proposes the send, and stops.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.933
In the console, Sophia opens the approval,

00:01:58.933 --> 00:02:02.900
reads the frozen message and the
claims panel, and approves or rejects.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:06.767
The proposer, and the human the
agent acts for, can never approve.

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:09.467
One habit worth copying:
send nothing at first.

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.967
In Dry Mode every send
becomes a logged draft,

00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:14.167
and each engine has its
own Dry or Live switch,

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.200
with the stricter one applying.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.300
New organizations start in Dry,
so read drafts, tune the voice,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.600
and send to an internal address first.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.833
Going live has its own
clip, Tutorial: going live.

00:02:24.867 --> 00:02:27.867
Third, sequences turn
one message into a plan.

00:02:27.867 --> 00:02:30.800
In the console: CRM,
Sequences, open one, Steps.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.200
You'll see ordered steps, waits
in the recipient's time zone,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.200
and weighted variants.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.600
Variants go to the same person
the same way every time.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.567
Edits mid flight never
send a message twice.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.533
A sequence ends for a person when
they reply, unsubscribe, bounce,

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:50.533
complain or are removed. A booked
meeting ends it by default.

00:02:50.533 --> 00:02:55.433
Or ask your agent: "Create a four
step funding sequence on my lane".

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.667
Signal plays connect the last
clips to this one. A funding,

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:04.600
hiring or intent signal enrols one
person into an approved sequence,

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.467
inside the daily cap.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:10.800
It skips customers, partners
and anyone who replied recently.

00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:14.800
Replies come back labelled: interested,
not now, objection, referral,

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.867
wrong person, unsubscribe,
out of office and bounce.

00:03:17.867 --> 00:03:21.167
In the console: CRM,
Conversations. Effects run once.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:24.467
An unsubscribe withdraws
consent, the record from Consent,

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.833
suppression and privacy.

00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:29.533
A bounce suppresses, and not now
creates a task for thirty days later.

00:03:29.533 --> 00:03:33.767
Or ask your agent: "What replies
came in and what do they want? "

00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:36.167
Meetings sit in the same engine.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:39.400
Booking and cancelling are
approval gated, like a send.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.433
Ask your agent: "Propose booking a
meeting with Priya Nair next Tuesday".

00:03:43.433 --> 00:03:45.967
A booked meeting ends the sequence.

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.600
Sequences can carry LinkedIn steps.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.867
They need a connected seat and haven't

00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:53.367
been verified against a real account yet,

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:57.067
so treat them as optional and test first.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:01.433
The dashboard shows replies by
channel, bounces, meetings booked,

00:04:01.433 --> 00:04:03.333
sends this week and contactability.

00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:08.667
What's working names winners only
once a group has thirty or more sends.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.800
In the console: Engines, Outreach, KPIs.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.467
Or ask your agent: "What is
working in our outreach? "

00:04:14.533 --> 00:04:17.133
What worked feeds the
next one to one draft,

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:20.667
and negative replies
lower the account's Score.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:24.100
Voice, proof, lanes, sequences and
reply labels are all definitions.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.933
Edit any of them through a ChangeSet,
and a different person signs it.

00:04:28.967 --> 00:04:32.633
Outreach reads Score to
decide who's worth a message.

00:04:32.633 --> 00:04:37.800
It reads Research for one to one
briefs, the proof library for claims,

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.600
and Routing for who owns the reply.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.133
Be clear about the limit.

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:45.800
The AI steps don't read wider
company context, only brand voice,

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.867
proof and customer phrases,
so keep your proof current.

00:04:48.867 --> 00:04:53.033
And some sender paths still wait
for tests against real accounts,

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:55.000
so send to an internal address first.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:58.167
The pushback: a person approving
every send won't scale.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.700
Approvers only see drafts
that already passed the gates,

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.700
with the claims verdicts
beside the message.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.400
The approval is bound to the exact
payload, so what they read is what goes.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.167
And the lane's daily
cap bounds the volume.

00:05:10.233 --> 00:05:14.500
The short version: Drafts are
grounded in your voice and proof,

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.900
lanes and gates shape every send,
and a second person approves it.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:22.867
Nothing goes out ungrounded,
and nothing goes out unapproved.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.333
Every draft is grounded,
every send is approved,

00:05:26.333 --> 00:05:30.967
and every reply teaches the system.
Read one lane's guardrails today.

00:05:30.967 --> 00:05:32.533
Next, SEO and GEO,

00:05:32.533 --> 00:05:37.000
where the same discipline decides
what goes live on your site.
